import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.C1oW5ckO.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"PumpkinPIE placeholders","description":"","frontmatter":{"editLink":"https://github.com/filiphsps/pumpkin-plugins/edit/master/packages/waypoints/docs/placeholders.md"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"packages/waypoints/docs/placeholders.md","filePath":"packages/waypoints/docs/placeholders.md","lastUpdated":1792068248000}`),a={name:`packages/waypoints/docs/placeholders.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="pumpkinpie-placeholders" tabindex="-1">PumpkinPIE placeholders <a class="header-anchor" href="#pumpkinpie-placeholders" aria-label="Permalink to “PumpkinPIE placeholders”">​</a></h1><p>Waypoints optionally registers the <code>waypoints</code> namespace with <a href="https://github.com/Rennex07/PumpkinPIE" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PumpkinPIE</a>. Install a compatible PumpkinPIE provider beside Waypoints to make these values available to other plugins. Without the provider, Waypoints still loads and its commands and Java HUD continue to work. The placeholders are server-side and do not depend on the viewer&#39;s Java or Bedrock edition or on a HUD being enabled.</p><p>Every lookup requires an online viewer resolved by the provider&#39;s current player <strong>name</strong>. UUIDs, name prefixes, console defaults and viewerless global queries are not accepted. Missing or offline viewers leave every Waypoints token unresolved, including public counts. The consuming server plugin supplies the viewer name; it is context for access checks, not end-user authentication. Treat this as trusted server-plugin integration, not as proof of who will see a message.</p><h2 id="access-and-selection" tabindex="-1">Access and selection <a class="header-anchor" href="#access-and-selection" aria-label="Permalink to “Access and selection”">​</a></h2><p>An accessible waypoint is enabled and passes Waypoints&#39; current access rules for the viewer. Public records are accessible to everyone; restricted records require a matching player UUID, permission node or <code>Waypoints:group.&lt;slug&gt;</code> marker. Operators bypass those grants, but disabled waypoints remain excluded. ACL changes, permission changes, movement and catalog edits affect the next lookup; the namespace uses no value cache.</p><p>“Here” means the viewer&#39;s exact current world key. Waypoints does not scale or compare coordinates between dimensions. Closest and nearest use accessible waypoints in that same world, regardless of HUD visibility range. Visible means eligible for the existing HUD projection: enabled, accessible, same world and inside the waypoint&#39;s optional 3D visibility range. It does not mean that a client currently sees a marker on screen; focus, fade, display edition and client state are not considered. Counts and lists only include records accessible to the supplied viewer. Waypoints does not publish a private-by-default raw total or aggregate hidden records.</p><p>Closest uses raw 3D distance. Nearest ranks use raw 3D distance before formatting and break exact ties by lowercase waypoint UUID in lexical order. Explicit UUID lookups can return authorized metadata from another world, but cross-world distances and directions are unresolved.</p><h2 id="catalog-values" tabindex="-1">Catalog values <a class="header-anchor" href="#catalog-values" aria-label="Permalink to “Catalog values”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%waypoints_count%</code></td><td>Accessible enabled waypoint count across all worlds.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_count_here%</code></td><td>Accessible enabled waypoint count in the current world.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_count_world:world%</code></td><td>Accessible enabled waypoint count in the exact argument world.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_public_count%</code></td><td>Accessible public-record count across all worlds.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_restricted_count%</code></td><td>Accessible restricted-record count across all worlds.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_visible_count%</code></td><td>Same-world count eligible for the HUD visibility range.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_nearby_count:128%</code></td><td>Same-world count within the 3D radius in blocks.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_names%</code></td><td>Accessible waypoint names across worlds, joined by comma and space.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_names_here%</code></td><td>Accessible same-world waypoint names, joined by comma and space.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Name lists sort by Waypoints&#39; normalized, case-insensitive name key, then UUID. They are display text, not escaped identifiers; waypoint names can contain commas. Disabled, denied and hidden-by-ACL records do not affect counts, names, existence checks or rank positions. A known empty name list resolves to an empty string.</p><h2 id="existence-lookups" tabindex="-1">Existence lookups <a class="header-anchor" href="#existence-lookups" aria-label="Permalink to “Existence lookups”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%waypoints_closest_exists%</code></td><td>Whether an accessible same-world closest waypoint exists.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_nearest_exists:2%</code></td><td>Whether the requested accessible same-world rank exists.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%waypoints_waypoint_exists:11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111%</code></td><td>Whether the enabled UUID is accessible to the viewer.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="waypoint-fields" tabindex="-1">Waypoint fields <a class="header-anchor" href="#waypoint-fields" aria-label="Permalink to “Waypoint fields”">​</a></h2><p>Substitute any field below in a closest, nearest or explicit UUID token. The same field rules apply to all three families.</p><p>| Field | Meaning | Output | | --- | --- | | <code>id</code> | Canonical waypoint UUID. | canonical lowercase UUID | | <code>name</code> | Complete saved waypoint name. | text | | <code>label</code> | Saved display label, falling back to the name. | text | | <code>description</code> | Saved description, or an empty string. | text | | <code>world</code> | Exact saved world key. | text | | <code>color</code> | Canonical waypoint color. | uppercase #RRGGBB | | <code>icon</code> | Canonical item ID, or an empty string. | item ID or empty | | <code>x</code> | Saved X coordinate. | locale-independent number; negative zero is 0 | | <code>y</code> | Saved Y coordinate. | locale-independent number; negative zero is 0 | | <code>z</code> | Saved Z coordinate. | locale-independent number; negative zero is 0 | | <code>distance</code> | Raw three-dimensional distance. | blocks to one decimal, no suffix | | <code>distance_horizontal</code> | Raw X/Z distance. | blocks to one decimal, no suffix | | <code>distance_formatted</code> | Human-readable distance. | rounded integer meters below 1000 blocks; otherwise one decimal kilometer | | <code>delta_x</code> | Destination X minus viewer X. | blocks to one decimal | | <code>delta_y</code> | Destination Y minus viewer Y. | blocks to one decimal | | <code>delta_z</code> | Destination Z minus viewer Z. | blocks to one decimal | | <code>bearing</code> | Horizontal compass bearing, north at zero. | degrees to one decimal | | <code>direction</code> | Eight-point compass direction. | N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW, UP, DOWN, or HERE | | <code>relative_direction</code> | Eight-point direction relative to the viewer yaw. | front, front_right, right, back_right, back, back_left, left, front_left, UP, DOWN, or HERE |</p><p>Compass sectors are 45 degrees wide; a boundary belongs to the clockwise sector. Relative direction uses the viewer&#39;s Minecraft yaw convention, where yaw zero faces south. If horizontal displacement is zero, bearing is a known empty string. Direction fields return <code>HERE</code> at the same position, <code>UP</code> above and <code>DOWN</code> below.</p><h2 id="token-forms-and-arguments" tabindex="-1">Token forms and arguments <a class="header-anchor" href="#token-forms-and-arguments" aria-label="Permalink to “Token forms and arguments”">​</a></h2><div class="language-text"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">text</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>%waypoints_closest_id%</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>%waypoints_nearest_id:2%</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>%waypoints_waypoint_id:11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111%</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>%waypoints_closest_exists%</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>%waypoints_nearest_exists:2%</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>%waypoints_waypoint_exists:11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111%</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>%waypoints_count_world:world%</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>%waypoints_nearby_count:128%</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Closest has no argument. Nearest requires a decimal integer rank from 1 through 100. UUID arguments must use the canonical hyphenated UUID shape; letter case is normalized. Unknown, disabled and inaccessible UUIDs all return <code>false</code> for <code>waypoint_exists</code>; metadata fields remain unresolved.</p><p>Catalog arguments:</p><ul><li><code>count_world</code> requires an exact, nonempty world key of at most 128 UTF-8 bytes.</li><li><code>nearby_count</code> requires a plain decimal radius greater than zero and at most 30,000,000 blocks. Exponent, hexadecimal, <code>Infinity</code> and <code>NaN</code> forms are rejected.</li><li><code>nearest_*</code> and <code>nearest_exists</code> require ranks from 1 through 100.</li><li><code>waypoint_*</code> and <code>waypoint_exists</code> require a canonical UUID.</li><li>All other tokens reject arguments.</li></ul><p>The PIE token grammar cannot represent every possible world key. For those keys, pass the world key as the separate API argument rather than embedding it in token text:</p><div class="language-ts"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">ts</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">import</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> { PieClient } </span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">from</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &#39;@pumpkin-plugins/pumpkin-pie-api&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">import</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> { ipcSend } </span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">from</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &#39;@pumpkin-plugins/plugin-kit/ipc&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">;</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">const</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> pie</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> =</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> new</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> PieClient</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(ipcSend);</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">pie.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">ping</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">();</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">const</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> count</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> =</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> pie.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">getValue</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&#39;waypoints_count_world&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&#39;Alex&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&#39;custom world key&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">);</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">const</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> line</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> =</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> pie.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">resolve</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&#39;Waypoints here: %waypoints_count_world%&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&#39;Alex&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&#39;world&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">);</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>getValue</code> preserves the distinction between <code>{ known: false }</code> and <code>{ known: true, value: &#39;&#39; }</code>. <code>resolve</code> and <code>resolveBatch</code> retain unresolved tokens in returned text and list their identifiers in <code>unresolved</code>. The caller sends resolved text through its own existing Pumpkin messaging API; PumpkinPIE resolves placeholders but does not deliver chat or UI messages.</p><h2 id="empty-unresolved-and-failed-values" tabindex="-1">Empty, unresolved and failed values <a class="header-anchor" href="#empty-unresolved-and-failed-values" aria-label="Permalink to “Empty, unresolved and failed values”">​</a></h2><p>Zero counts and distances are known values (<code>0</code> and <code>0.0</code>). A missing closest or valid nearest rank returns known empty strings for fields and <code>false</code> for existence checks. Missing optional description and icon metadata are known empty strings. Invalid arguments, unknown tokens, inaccessible or disabled explicit UUIDs, cross-world geometry, missing/offline viewers and values over 32 KiB UTF-8 remain unresolved. Storage and host-query failures also decline the value instead of returning a misleading zero or partial result.</p><p>The callback returns plain text only. It does not resolve nested tokens, escape markup, build text components or truncate oversized names. Waypoints logs a bounded identifier and reason once while a query failure remains active; stored waypoint text and host errors are never logged.</p><p>PumpkinPIE is optional. Provider retries use bounded exponential backoff capped at 5 minutes; after reaching the cap, probes are no more frequent than once every 5 minutes. A ready integration sends its registration heartbeat every 30 seconds and recovers automatically when PumpkinPIE becomes available.</p>`,28)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};